# Preflight Witnesses

No Block-04 target runner, cache, readiness theorem, direct-successor census,
formation-site law, axiom edit, obligation retirement, or TOE movement existed
before this registration.

Known inputs, not discoveries:

- The minimal axioms define a state as a configuration of permanent Records.
  Admissibility fixes a nearest-neighbor-conditioned possibility distribution
  conditional on formation, while explicitly leaving formation site and rate
  downstream.
- Source/Eta Block 03 constructs an exact one-event writer conditional on a
  target event and six neighboring Record values.  It explicitly does not
  supply autonomous eta preparation, a formation site/rate, or recurrence.
- If `x` is a valid six-Record target, each `x+d` occurs in the current Record
  domain.  This observation motivated the gate but is not yet registered as a
  general ready-set theorem.
- A nominal tuple `(eta_x,b,d)` fixes only the `-d` entry of a would-be mask at
  `x+d`; the other five entries require an extended physical state.
- Block 230 found a terminal-confluence failure for one frozen ACI rule and a
  live all-neighbor-readiness repair.  Block 231's full packed census is still
  running.  Block 232 remains staged/provisional and has independent open gaps
  in full-`M2` gluing, participant-sector ownership, and exact carrier
  certification.  None is imported as a completed theorem here.
- Gravity PR 7792 exactly resolves one supplied `q=3` vector-triple kernel into
  seven finite channels.  Its seven-channel temporal multiplier, arbitrary
  histories, invariant span, physical dynamics, continuum, and gravity bridge
  remain open.

The target novelty is the exact global partial-state typing theorem and the
decision it enables: whether the current Record-only one-event bridge can
propagate, merely consumes already-ready holes, or admits a counterexample.
Any broader no-go must fail closed under N1-N8 and be demoted if a live route
survives.
